    <section id="economic-nexus">
      <title>Changes to Economic Nexus Thresholds</title>
      <p>No changes to economic nexus thresholds in this release.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="tax-rates">
      <title>Changes to Tax Rates</title>
      <p><b>What changed:</b> Rate additions and updates by jurisdiction and tax type are
        summarized below.</p>

      <p outputclass="jurisdiction-heading"><b>US-MN-HENNEPIN-MPLS (Minneapolis, Minnesota /
        City — Hennepin County)</b></p>
      <dl outputclass="change-card">
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Tax Type</dt>
          <dd>Sales Tax</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Change Title</dt>
          <dd>Minneapolis Local Special District Tax Addition</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Citations</dt>
          <dd>MN Revenue Notice #26-04</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Effective From</dt>
          <dd>2026-07-01</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Additions</dt>
          <dd>New 0.5% local sales and use tax for the Minneapolis downtown special district.</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Summary</dt>
          <dd>A new 0.5% local sales and use tax has been enacted for the Minneapolis downtown
            special district.</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Impact</dt>
          <dd>Total sales tax for eligible downtown transactions will increase to 9.025%.</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Tax Codes</dt>
          <dd>Addition — MN-MPLS-DT (Downtown District Surcharge)</dd>
        </dlentry>
      </dl>
      <note type="attention" outputclass="action-required">
        <b>Action Required:</b> Ensure your point-of-sale systems are configured to pass the
        accurate address or latitude/longitude for downtown Minneapolis locations.
      </note>

      <p outputclass="jurisdiction-heading"><b>US-VA-NORFOLK (Norfolk, Virginia / Independent
        City)</b></p>
      <dl outputclass="change-card">
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Tax Type</dt>
          <dd>Lodging Tax</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Change Title</dt>
          <dd>Norfolk Nightly Lodging Fee Update</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Citations</dt>
          <dd>Norfolk Ordinance 12-345</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Effective From</dt>
          <dd>2026-01-01</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Updates</dt>
          <dd>Tax base for the $3 fee changed from Per Night to Per Night Per Number of Rooms.</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Summary</dt>
          <dd>Tax base for $3 fee changed from Per Night to Per Night Per Number of Rooms.</dd>
        </dlentry>
      </dl>
      <note type="attention" outputclass="action-required">
        <b>Action Required:</b> Provide room count for stays on or after Jan 1.
      </note>
    </section>

    <section id="taxability-rules">
      <title>Changes to Taxability Rules</title>
      <p><b>What changed:</b> The following jurisdiction had a change to the taxable base logic
        underlying an existing tax type.</p>
      <p outputclass="jurisdiction-heading"><b>Bloomington, Minnesota (City) — Hennepin County</b></p>
      <dl outputclass="change-card">
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Tax Type</dt>
          <dd>Admissions Tax</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Change Title</dt>
          <dd>Mall of America Admissions Tax Adjustment</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Citations</dt>
          <dd>Bloomington City Ord. 2026-11</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Updates</dt>
          <dd>Minor adjustment to the taxable base for entertainment admissions within the Mall
            of America district.</dd>
        </dlentry>
        <dlentry>
          <dt>Impact</dt>
          <dd>Admissions tax calculations for affected venues within the district will reflect
            the revised taxable base.</dd>
        </dlentry>
      </dl>
    </section>

